You are operating directly inside ZCoder after Upgrade-22.

================================================================
MISSION
================================================================

Upgrade-22 reportedly completed the durable engineering fleet:

- SQLite WAL durability
- PostgreSQL distributed coordination
- subprocess crash recovery
- multi-process worker contention
- RLS
- repository portfolio
- engineering campaigns
- worker fleet
- campaign scheduler
- durable recovery

Upgrade-23 must make that fleet INTELLIGENT.

Current system can execute work.

Upgrade-23 answers:

"What work should we do next, and why?"

Target:

Repository Portfolio
        │
        ▼
Evidence Collectors
        │
        ├── Git
        ├── CI
        ├── Dependency manifests
        ├── Test baselines
        ├── Security advisories
        ├── Runtime/support metadata
        └── Project configuration
        │
        ▼
Maintenance Intelligence Engine
        │
        ├── Dependency Graph
        ├── CI Failure Clustering
        ├── Risk Scoring
        ├── Staleness Detection
        ├── Repository Health
        └── Opportunity Detection
        │
        ▼
Recommendation Engine
        │
        ▼
Campaign Planner
        │
        ├── CI repair
        ├── security remediation
        ├── dependency maintenance
        ├── test maintenance
        ├── documentation
        └── repository hygiene
        │
        ▼
Upgrade-22 Durable Engineering Fleet

The intelligence layer recommends and plans.

The existing engineering runtime executes.

Do NOT build another execution engine.

================================================================
PHASE 0 — FINAL UPGRADE-22 RELEASE AUDIT
================================================================

Before adding intelligence, independently verify the Upgrade-22
foundation.

Run:

git status --short
git log -40 --oneline
git tag --sort=-version:refname | head -30

python -m pytest -q -ra
python main.py --version
python -m build
git diff --check

Run all current release gates.

Verify separately:

SQLite durability
real subprocess restart
hard crash recovery
PostgreSQL integration
multi-process task claiming
RLS
stale worker fencing
real Git repository
real git worktree
real commit
local bare remote
operation reconciliation
campaign restart
fleet fairness

Produce:

UPGRADE-22 FINAL FOUNDATION MATRIX

Capability
Implementation
Execution Evidence
Evidence Tier
Required Skip?
Verdict

Do not begin Upgrade-23 implementation if a P0 durability or tenant
isolation regression exists.

================================================================
1. RELEASE VERSION TRUTH
================================================================

The repository has accumulated many major subsystems under v1.40.0.

Inspect actual:

Git tags
package metadata
release metadata
wheel version

Determine whether 1.40.0 is:

UNRELEASED DEVELOPMENT
PRE-RELEASE
PUBLISHED RELEASE

If it has already been published:

select a new SemVer.

Do not mutate an already released immutable version indefinitely.

================================================================
2. MAINTENANCE INTELLIGENCE DOMAIN
================================================================

Create:

MaintenanceIntelligenceService

Responsibilities:

collect evidence
normalize signals
calculate repository health
identify maintenance opportunities
rank recommendations
create campaign proposals

It MUST NOT directly mutate repositories.

================================================================
3. EVIDENCE FIRST
================================================================

Every recommendation needs:

recommendation
reason
source evidence
confidence
risk
estimated scope

No recommendation may be:

"AI thinks this is probably useful"

without evidence.

================================================================
4. MAINTENANCE SIGNAL
================================================================

Create:

MaintenanceSignal

Fields conceptually:

id
repository
type
severity
source
evidence
detected_at
freshness
confidence
status

================================================================
5. SIGNAL TYPES
================================================================

Initial signals:

CI_FAILURE
TEST_FAILURE
LINT_FAILURE
TYPECHECK_FAILURE
BUILD_FAILURE

DEPENDENCY_OUTDATED
DEPENDENCY_SECURITY
DEPENDENCY_UNPINNED

UNSUPPORTED_RUNTIME
STALE_CONFIGURATION

DOCUMENTATION_STALE

SECURITY_FINDING

REPOSITORY_INACTIVE
REPOSITORY_HEALTH_DEGRADED

================================================================
6. SIGNAL IS NOT TASK
================================================================

Signal:

"dependency is outdated"

does not automatically mean:

"update dependency"

The Recommendation Engine decides whether action is justified.

================================================================
7. SIGNAL FRESHNESS
================================================================

Track:

FRESH
STALE
UNKNOWN

Do not prioritize stale evidence as if current.

================================================================
8. EVIDENCE PROVENANCE
================================================================

Every signal records source.

Examples:

package.json
pyproject.toml
GitHub Actions
test baseline
advisory database
Git history

================================================================
9. REPOSITORY DEPENDENCY INVENTORY
================================================================

Build normalized dependency inventory.

Support at minimum detected ecosystems already understood by ZCoder.

Examples:

Python
Node/TypeScript

Extensible architecture for:

Go
Rust
Java
others

================================================================
10. DEPENDENCY RECORD
================================================================

Fields:

ecosystem
name
declared_constraint
resolved_version
source_manifest
lockfile
direct_or_transitive
development_dependency
evidence

================================================================
11. DIRECT VS TRANSITIVE
================================================================

Keep distinct.

Do not propose editing direct manifest for a purely transitive issue
without understanding resolution mechanism.

================================================================
12. LOCKFILE EVIDENCE
================================================================

Use actual lockfiles when present.

Do not infer resolved dependency version from declared range only.

================================================================
13. PACKAGE MANAGER
================================================================

Reuse Upgrade-19 package manager detection.

No duplicated detector.

================================================================
14. DEPENDENCY GRAPH
================================================================

Create:

DependencyGraph

Nodes:

repositories
packages
internal artifacts

Edges:

DEPENDS_ON
DEV_DEPENDS_ON
BUILDS_FROM
CONSUMES_ARTIFACT

================================================================
15. EVIDENCE-BACKED EDGES
================================================================

Every dependency edge records source evidence.

Do not infer:

repo-name similarity
→ dependency.

================================================================
16. INTERNAL REPOSITORY DEPENDENCY
================================================================

Detect internal dependencies where clear evidence exists.

Examples:

workspace configuration
package reference
path dependency
internal package coordinates

================================================================
17. GRAPH CONFIDENCE
================================================================

Use:

HIGH
MEDIUM
LOW

Do not treat low-confidence graph edges as hard ordering constraints.

================================================================
18. DEPENDENCY CYCLES
================================================================

Graph may contain cycles.

Algorithms must tolerate them.

================================================================
19. IMPACT ANALYSIS
================================================================

When dependency/repository changes:

identify evidence-backed downstream repositories.

Do not claim complete blast-radius detection unless proven.

================================================================
20. OUTDATED DEPENDENCY DETECTOR
================================================================

Create provider-neutral dependency version intelligence.

Do not hardcode one commercial service.

================================================================
21. CURRENT VERSION
================================================================

Determine current installed/resolved version from repository evidence.

================================================================
22. AVAILABLE VERSION
================================================================

External lookup is optional/provider-backed.

If network unavailable:

status:

VERSION_LOOKUP_UNAVAILABLE

not:

UP_TO_DATE.

================================================================
23. NO RANDOM SCRAPING
================================================================

Use official ecosystem registries/APIs where integration exists.

================================================================
24. VERSION POLICY
================================================================

Classify available update:

PATCH
MINOR
MAJOR
PRERELEASE
UNKNOWN

================================================================
25. DEFAULT UPDATE POLICY
================================================================

No-cost maintenance default:

PATCH_ONLY

unless project configuration specifies otherwise.

================================================================
26. MAJOR UPDATE
================================================================

Never create automatic major-upgrade campaign without explicit policy.

================================================================
27. PRERELEASE
================================================================

Do not recommend prerelease upgrade by default.

================================================================
28. PINNING INTELLIGENCE
================================================================

Detect:

exact pin
range
unpinned
floating/latest-like configuration

Do not assume exact pin is always best.

Report policy implication.

================================================================
29. STALE DEPENDENCY
================================================================

Separate:

OUTDATED

from:

VULNERABLE.

They have different priority.

================================================================
30. SECURITY ADVISORY PROVIDER
================================================================

Create:

AdvisoryProvider

No-cost/open provider first.

Commercial scanners remain optional adapters.

================================================================
31. ADVISORY RECORD
================================================================

Normalize:

ecosystem
package
affected range
fixed versions
severity
identifier
source
published/modified
reference

================================================================
32. NO FALSE VULNERABILITY MATCH
================================================================

Match against actual resolved dependency version where possible.

Do not mark package vulnerable simply because advisory mentions package
name.

================================================================
33. UNKNOWN RESOLUTION
================================================================

If exact installed version cannot be determined:

VULNERABILITY_STATUS_UNKNOWN

not vulnerable-by-default.

================================================================
34. ADVISORY DEDUPLICATION
================================================================

Multiple sources may describe same issue.

Normalize identifiers where possible.

Do not inflate risk score by counting duplicate advisories.

================================================================
35. SECURITY SEVERITY
================================================================

Preserve source severity.

Do not invent CVSS scores.

================================================================
36. FIX AVAILABILITY
================================================================

Distinguish:

FIX_AVAILABLE
NO_FIX
UNKNOWN

================================================================
37. SECURITY RECOMMENDATION
================================================================

High-severity + fix available:

strong candidate for remediation campaign.

Still require:

project compatibility
policy
validation

================================================================
38. SECURITY CAMPAIGN PRIORITY
================================================================

Security may outrank ordinary maintenance.

But critical project policy/approval still applies.

================================================================
39. CI INTELLIGENCE
================================================================

Upgrade CI discovery into:

CIFailureIntelligenceService

================================================================
40. CI FAILURE RECORD
================================================================

Normalize:

repository
workflow
job
step
commit
failure class
message fingerprint
timestamp

================================================================
41. FAILURE TAXONOMY
================================================================

Classify:

TEST
LINT
TYPECHECK
BUILD
DEPENDENCY
CONFIGURATION
SECURITY
INFRASTRUCTURE
FLAKE
UNKNOWN

================================================================
42. DO NOT FIX INFRA FAILURE AS CODE
================================================================

Infrastructure outage must not automatically generate code repair.

================================================================
43. FAILURE FINGERPRINT
================================================================

Create deterministic fingerprint using bounded normalized evidence.

================================================================
44. CI FAILURE CLUSTERING
================================================================

Group identical/similar failures across:

runs
branches
repositories

Start deterministic.

Do not require embedding/LLM clustering.

================================================================
45. CROSS-REPO FAILURE CLUSTER
================================================================

Example:

20 repos fail because shared CI action version broke.

Recognize common pattern where evidence supports it.

================================================================
46. CLUSTER CONFIDENCE
================================================================

Report:

HIGH
MEDIUM
LOW

================================================================
47. ROOT-CAUSE CANDIDATE
================================================================

Cluster may nominate likely common cause.

Label:

CANDIDATE

not confirmed root cause unless evidence proves it.

================================================================
48. FLAKE INTELLIGENCE
================================================================

Track recurring test failures with inconsistent outcomes.

Do not label a test flaky from one failure.

================================================================
49. FLAKE EVIDENCE
================================================================

Require repeated history.

================================================================
50. BASELINE INTELLIGENCE
================================================================

Reuse repository baseline history.

Track:

test status
lint
typecheck
build

over time.

================================================================
51. HEALTH TREND
================================================================

Create trend:

IMPROVING
STABLE
DEGRADING
UNKNOWN

Based on evidence.

================================================================
52. REPOSITORY HEALTH MODEL V2
================================================================

Health dimensions:

BUILD
TEST
CI
SECURITY
DEPENDENCIES
MAINTENANCE
READINESS

================================================================
53. HEALTH HARD GATES
================================================================

Critical security failure cannot be hidden by green documentation score.

================================================================
54. HEALTH SUMMARY
================================================================

Top-level:

HEALTHY
DEGRADED
FAILING
CRITICAL
UNKNOWN

================================================================
55. HEALTH SCORE
================================================================

Optional numerical score.

Always expose dimensions.

================================================================
56. MAINTENANCE DEBT
================================================================

Create evidence-backed maintenance debt signals.

Examples:

persistent CI red
very stale patch dependencies
deprecated runtime
known security issues
repeated repair failures

Do not invent financial "debt cost."

================================================================
57. REPOSITORY AGE IS NOT DEBT
================================================================

An old stable repository may be healthy.

Do not penalize age alone.

================================================================
58. ENGINEERING RECOMMENDATION
================================================================

Create:

MaintenanceRecommendation

Fields:

id
repository/campaign scope
type
priority
risk
confidence
reason
evidence
estimated files/repositories
proposed campaign
status

================================================================
59. RECOMMENDATION TYPES
================================================================

Examples:

REPAIR_CI
PATCH_DEPENDENCY
SECURITY_REMEDIATION
UPDATE_RUNTIME
FIX_TESTS
IMPROVE_VALIDATION
REFRESH_DOCUMENTATION
NO_ACTION

================================================================
60. NO_ACTION IS VALID
================================================================

Intelligence system must be capable of deciding:

no maintenance action recommended.

================================================================
61. PRIORITY MODEL
================================================================

Priority inputs:

security severity
CI/build impact
project policy
repository health
dependency blast radius
confidence
age/freshness
repair history

================================================================
62. PRIORITY IS EXPLAINABLE
================================================================

Never output opaque priority number alone.

================================================================
63. BUSINESS CRITICALITY
================================================================

Use only if explicitly configured.

Do not infer business importance from repository stars/activity.

================================================================
64. RISK MODEL
================================================================

Risk considers:

scope
major version change
workflow/deployment files
security-sensitive code
dependency blast radius
historical repair failure

================================================================
65. RECOMMENDATION CONFIDENCE
================================================================

Confidence derives from evidence quality.

Not LLM certainty.

================================================================
66. RECOMMENDATION EXPLAIN
================================================================

CLI/API should show:

why
evidence
risk
confidence
affected repos
suggested campaign

================================================================
67. MAINTENANCE PLANNER
================================================================

Create:

MaintenancePlanner

Turns approved recommendations into EngineeringCampaign proposals.

================================================================
68. PLAN ONLY BY DEFAULT
================================================================

Intelligence should not automatically run campaign merely because it
found issue.

Default:

recommend
→ plan
→ explicit run/policy

================================================================
69. SAFE AUTO-MAINTENANCE
================================================================

Optional policy may auto-run selected low-risk campaign types.

Example:

documentation
patch dependency

only under explicit configuration.

================================================================
70. NO AUTO-MAJOR
================================================================

Hard invariant unless explicit override.

================================================================
71. CAMPAIGN DEDUPLICATION
================================================================

Same open recommendation must not generate repeated identical campaign.

================================================================
72. CAMPAIGN SUPERSESSION
================================================================

New evidence may supersede old recommendation.

Track history.

================================================================
73. RECOMMENDATION STATES
================================================================

NEW
ACKNOWLEDGED
PLANNED
RUNNING
RESOLVED
DISMISSED
STALE
SUPERSEDED

================================================================
74. RESOLUTION VERIFICATION
================================================================

Do not mark recommendation RESOLVED because commit exists.

Recollect evidence.

Verify condition disappeared.

================================================================
75. POST-CAMPAIGN VERIFICATION
================================================================

Example dependency security issue:

campaign succeeds
→ rerun dependency/advisory analysis
→ advisory no longer matches
→ RESOLVED

================================================================
76. FAILED MAINTENANCE
================================================================

Campaign failure updates recommendation evidence.

Do not loop endlessly.

================================================================
77. REPAIRABILITY HISTORY
================================================================

Track:

attempt count
historical success
failure category

Use in future planning.

================================================================
78. CAMPAIGN RECOMMENDATION ENGINE
================================================================

Examples:

10 repos same CI failure
→ one campaign proposal

5 repos vulnerable dependency
→ security campaign

Do not manually require per-repo task creation.

================================================================
79. CROSS-REPO CONSOLIDATION
================================================================

Combine recommendations only when action is sufficiently similar.

================================================================
80. DIFFERENT PACKAGE MANAGERS
================================================================

Same dependency issue across npm/Python ecosystems does NOT imply same
campaign implementation.

================================================================
81. CAMPAIGN TEMPLATE VERSIONING
================================================================

Recommendation references exact campaign template version.

================================================================
82. INTELLIGENCE WITHOUT LLM
================================================================

All core detection/ranking must operate without model inference.

No-cost mode remains functional if no LLM daemon exists.

================================================================
83. OPTIONAL LOCAL LLM ENRICHMENT
================================================================

Optional local model may:

summarize evidence
generate human-readable explanation
suggest investigation

It cannot override deterministic security/policy findings.

================================================================
84. NO LLM AS VULNERABILITY SCANNER
================================================================

Never infer vulnerability solely from model output.

================================================================
85. NO LLM VERSION INVENTION
================================================================

Package versions come from registries/manifests, not language model.

================================================================
86. NO LLM CI STATUS INVENTION
================================================================

CI evidence must come from provider/local records.

================================================================
87. PORTFOLIO INTELLIGENCE
================================================================

Aggregate:

repo health
CI failure clusters
security exposure
dependency update opportunities
campaign state
engineering throughput

================================================================
88. PORTFOLIO PRIORITY QUEUE
================================================================

Show recommended maintenance ordered by explicit priority policy.

================================================================
89. PORTFOLIO RISK MAP
================================================================

Group repositories:

CRITICAL
HIGH
MEDIUM
LOW

with reasons.

Do not fabricate heatmap metrics.

================================================================
90. DEPENDENCY BLAST RADIUS
================================================================

For internal package change:

show known downstream repositories.

================================================================
91. SHARED FAILURE INTELLIGENCE
================================================================

If same failure cluster affects many repositories:

surface shared remediation candidate.

================================================================
92. CAMPAIGN SAVINGS
================================================================

Do not fabricate monetary savings.

May report:

repositories affected
tasks avoided
duplicate investigation avoided

based on actual counts.

================================================================
93. MAINTENANCE WINDOW
================================================================

Recommendation may respect repository/campaign maintenance policies.

================================================================
94. INTERACTIVE WORK PRECEDENCE
================================================================

Maintenance intelligence should not overwhelm interactive engineering
queue.

================================================================
95. STALE RECOMMENDATIONS
================================================================

Re-evaluate before campaign starts.

================================================================
96. REPOSITORY CHANGED
================================================================

If manifest/HEAD materially changed after recommendation:

revalidate evidence.

================================================================
97. ADVISORY UPDATE
================================================================

Changed advisory can invalidate recommendation.

================================================================
98. INTELLIGENCE CACHE
================================================================

Cache provider results responsibly.

Track freshness.

================================================================
99. OFFLINE MODE
================================================================

Offline intelligence supports:

repository analysis
stored dependency data
CI history
local health
existing advisory cache

External latest lookup unavailable.

Report it.

================================================================
