## 32. Final Verdict

Never label package CURRENT if registry lookup failed.

Never claim vulnerability from package name alone.

Never call a CI infrastructure outage a code regression without evidence.

Never recommend a major dependency upgrade automatically.

Never generate maintenance work merely to keep agents busy.

Never use an LLM's opinion as the authoritative security finding.

Never allow maintenance intelligence to bypass Upgrade-22 campaign
safety, approval, canary, fencing or zero-cost policies.

Upgrade-23 succeeds when ZCoder not only executes engineering work
reliably, but can determine — from evidence — which maintenance work is
actually worth doing next.